WEBVTT

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.760
Setsu.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.400
If I die, stop playing the shamisen.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.040
How does this sound?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.300
You can stay here till you find out what
you wanna do and where you wanna go.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.150
Tachiki Yuna

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:16.070
I thought you were like me,
a sad person with nothing going for you.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.200
That's why I let you stay.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.240
But now...

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.240
I'm jealous of you.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.210
I quit my agency.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.000
I was always empty,
right from the very start.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.910
<i>Yuna-san...</i>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.460
<i>The one who has nothing...</i>

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.200
<i>...is me.</i>

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.480
Why aren't you gonna be in the
competition? I wanted to beat you!

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.730
<i>I can't hear Gramps' sound...</i>

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.220
You keep running away!

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.480
That's why I can't get my father's approval!

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.850
<i>That skin-pricking...</i>

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.150
I'm not interested.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.980
<i>...cold and painful place.</i>

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.480
Gramps' sound is the only
thing I'm interested in.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.050
So you're finally awake, huh?

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.950
Setsu.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:29.480
Those Snow

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:29.480
White Notes

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.760
U-Umeko?

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.550
Episode 2
Apple Blossoms

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.890
<i>Wait, how... Why is Umeko...</i>

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.770
*Knocked Setsu out with tear gas.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.860
<i>I was at Yuna-san's place, and...</i>

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.440
I found out you'd gone to Tokyo.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.230
Look at me! You <i>will</i> tell me where Setsu is!

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.870
As your mother,
I couldn't let you fend for yourself.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.780
You'll live here from now on.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.160
What's this all about?

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.500
You haven't done a single
motherly thing in your life...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.330
Welcome! Step right up!

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:12.040
You're right. I foisted my kids on Matsugoro
and hightailed it out of Tsugaru.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.040
And now, Matsugoro's dead...

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.720
Setsu, why did you leave Tsugaru?

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.790
Uh, well...

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.530
When Gramps died,
my sound disappeared, too.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.880
Oh, yeah? How far's it gone?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.020
"Tsugaru Ohara Bushi." Let's go.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.390
And listen up.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.450
I will not tolerate disgraceful
playing accompanying my singing.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.230
Don't dampen the sound, you hear?

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.300
You'll finish it off with a solo.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.370
Make everyone down there turn and look.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.870
<i>"Tsugaru Ohara Bushi."</i>

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.840
<i>It reflects Tsugaru's four seasons
through the imagery of an apple tree.</i>

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.010
<i>But it can also be interpreted...</i>

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.680
<i>as a metaphor for stages in a woman's life.</i>

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.590
<i>Fresh and unsullied,
with a deep, quiet strength.</i>

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.310
<i>It was a song Gramps played often.</i>

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:28.110
<i>в™« Saa в™« </i>

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:36.960
<i>в™« Ah в™« </i>

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.130
<i>в™« Ah, ah, saa в™« </i>

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:54.970
<i>в™« Now we begin в™« </i>

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.710
<i>I hate my mom.</i>

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.020
<i>But her voice...</i>

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.610
<i>Whenever I hear her sing,
it makes my heart tremble.</i>

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:12.730
<i>в™« Ah, even the apple trees on wintry days в™« </i>

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:20.090
<i>в™« repose with their limbs buried in snow в™« </i>

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:27.420
<i>в™« awaiting the moment their buds emerge в™« </i>

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.240
<i>Matsugoro's blood flows
in your veins.</i>

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.680
<i>Is that all you've got?</i>

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:56.870
<i>в™« Ah, in spring, they are
delicately, deftly pruned в™« </i>

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:04.130
<i>в™« Wearing medicinal herbs as makeup,
they revisit their youth в™« </i>

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.880
<i>Umeko's voice is overpowering my sound!</i>

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:11.640
<i>в™« These flowers blossom but once a year в™« </i>

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:11.640
<i>Gramps...</i>

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.910
<i>Gramps' "Ohara Bushi"...</i>

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:32.170
<i>в™« Ah, when autumn comes and
it shows its face once more в™« </i>

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:38.670
<i>в™« it has ripened and taken
on a luscious red hue в™« </i>

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:34.350
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.880
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:46.680
<i>в™« and its taste is even finer than its color в™« </i>

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:44.100
<i>The apple blossoms danced and
the scent of apples filled the air</i>

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.750
<i>for Matsugoro's "Ohara Bushi," too.</i>

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:08.200
<i>This really is going to
turn into something incredible.</i>

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.270
Wh-Why...

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:16.250
How could you let the song end like <i>that</i>?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.690
What're you gonna do
about this fire inside me?

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.250
You're leaving me all pent-up!

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.710
What Ow!

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.070
What was I meant to do? I didn't have
the money to replace the strings!

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:26.380
This is why I hate poor people!

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.360
Huh?

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.280
Hey!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.540
Was that you singing just now?

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:33.390
Yeah.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.890
So that young man was your accompanist, huh?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.640
I'll give you croquettes on the
house! Come grab 'em later!

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.080
Hey, kid!

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.800
You can come play at my
boarding house whenever you like.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.810
Treat us to another song sometime!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.450
<i>Looks like it was a success.</i>

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.170
Now you can practice all
you want without worrying.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.390
Your high school uniform and stuff.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.790
Huh? Wait, I

00:07:58.700 --> 00:07:59.790
I will not wait.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:03.130
If you want to live in Tokyo,
I'll be your legal guardian.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.920
I don't need high school

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.250
Don't try running. It's no use.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.630
And Wakana will accompany
you on your first day.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.970
I've no idea who that child takes after.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.170
He's diligent and always
looking out for people.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:18.120
Even though he mumbled that
he didn't care what happens to you,

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.640
he said he'd come out here,
even though no one asked.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:24.690
In any case, I hate men with no education.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.360
If you don't like it, go back to Aomori.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:37.640
<i>I have no purpose here in Tokyo.</i>

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.000
<i>A boarding house in Tokyo's old town...</i>

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.960
<i>Going to high school...</i>

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.800
<i>Just drifting along, going with the flow...</i>

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.770
<i>What am I even doing?</i>

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.680
Ta

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.680
nukichi

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.680
Din

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.680
er

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.550
Morning Horoscope Corner

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:59.660
<i>Now, for the first day of Golden Week,
the luckiest sign of them all is:</i>

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:02.170
<i>Capricorn!</i>

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:06.030
<i>Even if a person makes you feel awkward,
talk honestly about how you feel.</i>

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:09.370
<i>I'm sure you'll get to see a side
of them you don't usually see.</i>

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:10.150
The mood seems a little
heavy over there, doesn't it?

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:11.800
<i>Your lucky item is a musical instrument!</i>

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.560
It's a testing time for fathers
when their kid gets to that age.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:17.450
<i>And our unluckiest sign is:
sorry, guys, it's Taurus.</i>

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.260
He's the older brother, apparently.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.210
What?!

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:19.300
With a bearing as dignified as his,
he looks like he should have kids!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.270
<i>Lately, your luck has been on a downturn,</i>

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.910
<i>but give a gift to someone you like,
and something good may happen!</i>

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.200
Or at least a lover or two

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:26.400
<i>Your lucky item is a red handkerchief.</i>

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:26.380
Setsu, why aren't you saying anything?

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.590
What about you, Wakana-chan?

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.760
<i>With clear skies across the country,</i>

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:31.620
Why aren't you saying anything
about me leaving home?

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.010
<i>it looks like it'll be a lovely
day for all of us today.</i>

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:36.080
<i>But in the Kanto region,
evening brings with it a chance of rain,</i>

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:34.920
Well...

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:39.080
I have so much I want to say,
I don't even know where to start!

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.910
<i>so don't forget to pack your umbrellas!</i>

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.310
<i>So, everyone, let's go do
our best for another day!</i>

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:41.310
Do you have <i>any</i> idea how worried I've been?

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.890
You wanna know the secret behind my beauty?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.680
This is it: Umemaru moisturizing gel cream.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.100
With this...

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.740
<i>...my skin stays soft and springy all day long.</i>

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.580
Wrinkles and dullness.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.300
Dryness.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.560
Don't ever give up on yourself.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:03.590
Oh! That was Setsu-san's mother.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:08.140
I knew she wasn't your average person, but...
So she's some kind of TV star, huh?

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.620
She isn't a TV star.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.640
That's just how Umeko is.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.980
This necktie's annoying. I'm taking it off.

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:21.050
Leave it alone, idiot. You'll make
a bad impression on your first day.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:25.670
Honestly. I rush here from the competition
and <i>this</i> is what I have to deal with...

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:28.840
Wakana-chan, why are you
so proper about everything?

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:31.560
Because, little brother, <i>you</i> are
too half-assed about everything!

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.450
Did you say competition?

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.390
The National Shamisen
Tournament in Hirosaki.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:36.720
Wow.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:38.610
How did you do?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.960
I managed to get third.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:42.320
That's amazing.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.940
No, it's not.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:44.720
Huh?

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.040
A lot of players come
from all different styles.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.340
Yeah, that's true.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:53.180
Two-time champ, Ogata Kousuke, is an
accredited master from the Kamiki School.

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:57.260
Second went to his junior from the
same school: Tanuma Souichi, a third-year.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:58.920
Tanuma?

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:02.470
Souichi's little sister was in
the same year as you, right?

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:03.560
Remember her?

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.180
Coward!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.900
Yeah, you remember.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:12.050
His little sister won in
the women's division.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.730
She had no trouble remembering you.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:16.780
What?

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.150
39th

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.150
<b>Tsugaru Shamisen National Tournament</b>

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.150
What do you mean he left?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.480
Setsu's gone to Tokyo.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.080
He isn't in Aomori anymore.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:27.200
He's never been interested in
competing against others, anyway.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.740
He likely won't come to future compet

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.390
Oh! Are you shocked?

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.760
Does this mean you were in love with Setsu?

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.430
You're no match for the Kamiki School!

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.930
There's no way you'll beat my big brother!

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:48.270
Tanuma's little sister, Mai, was dead right.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:54.150
That hall was filled with sound so intense,
it felt like your heart would burst.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.890
At just eighteen years old,

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:02.290
Tanuma Souichi gave
a staggering performance.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:04.920
I was jealous.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:06.920
No...

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:08.840
I was utterly defeated.

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.080
A hole opened up in my heart.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.170
I'll never match him.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.190
No matter how much emotion
you put into your music,

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.000
if you're bad at it, you're bad.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:23.330
This is probably as far as I can go.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:32.180
<i>Wakana-chan and I grew up
listening to Gramps' sound.</i>

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:38.770
<i>When we lost the person who raised us,
we also lost our teacher.</i>

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:43.400
<i>We've both hit a brick wall,
stuck in the dark.</i>

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.290
<i>I've looked up to him for
as long as I can remember,</i>

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:53.750
<i>and I've been chasing Gramps' impromptu piece,
"Shungyou (Spring Dawn)," this whole time.</i>

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:59.790
<i>Gramps, what was it about the dawn
that made you feel spring?</i>

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.130
<i>Well, Gramps?</i>

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:10.810
Everyone, meet your new friend,
Sawamura Setsu-kun.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.810
Sawamura
Setsu

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.070
Setsu-kun, would you like to say something?

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.470
He's kinda hot, isn't he?

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.070
Right?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:14.890
Nice t'meet you.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.310
Thank you. Applause, everyone!

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.310
Was that an accent just now?

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.400
Yeah.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.560
Things must have been
very difficult for Setsu-kun.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:22.240
Difficult?

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.420
Not being able to attend
high school in Aomori

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:27.200
because he had to look after
his sick grandfather, I mean.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.200
<i>What?</i>

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.410
And the exhaustion caused
his own flu to worsen,

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.370
sending him to the hospital for a long time,
where he hovered between life and death.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:40.460
His mother sobbed as she told us all about it.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.840
I was crying in sympathy.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.600
Speaking of sympathy, she donated
a considerable sum of money to our school.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.810
A marvel of a mother, wouldn't you agree?

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:50.390
Ah, yeah...

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.190
<i>That devious vixen.</i>

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.190
Were you nervous?

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.830
All you said in your introduction
was "nice t'meet you."

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:57.560
Not really.

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:59.960
Just tell me if you have
anything on your mind, okay?

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:02.190
As your teacher, I'll do what I can to help!

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.440
Right...

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.860
Koyabu-sensei.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.420
Oh, Maeda-san.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:14.480
Will you look this over to make sure
your contact information is correct?

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:15.950
So what's wrong?

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.840
Well... This has been in the
music prep room since forever.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.380
Would it be okay if I used it?

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.210
What is it?

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:28.430
I think it's a thick-necked
futozao-style Tsugaru shamisen.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:31.730
Oh, for the shamisen appreciation club?

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:34.140
You're working hard all on
your own there, aren't you?

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.290
Yes.

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:38.460
When I asked the music teacher,
I was told that an alumnus

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:41.400
called Ogata Kousuke had left it there.

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.190
Hm?

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:46.600
What...

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:48.680
What <i>is</i> all this?

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:52.170
It's broken down into pieces.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.200
Really? What for?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:58.450
That seems like a lot of trouble.
It would fit just fine without doing that.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:02.630
I'd rather people didn't mess with
stuff they don't know anything about.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:03.260
Huh?

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:04.200
Pardon?

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.150
Here.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.800
Is it wrong for me... to touch it?

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.420
Why ask me?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.300
I'm not just messing with it.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:18.570
But I don't know what to do next...

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:20.810
so I guess I shouldn't use it, huh?

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:25.270
Take it out of the bag.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.520
What's this?

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:32.360
The skin is ripped!

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:35.000
The skin is a living thing.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.910
It's like this because no air
got to it for a long time.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.440
What are they doing?

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.470
They're putting together a shamisen.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:00.270
Here.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:02.360
It's a nice one and no mistake.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.070
It's beautiful...

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.320
Yeah, it is.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:14.410
The grain here flows beautifully.
It's red sandalwood.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.990
I'm sure it will sound amazing.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.580
Sensei! Please allow me to use this!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:26.600
I'll work really hard to find more
members for the Tsugaru shamisen club!

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:29.380
Replacing the skin will
set you back 40 or 50k.

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:33.600
All right, I'll look after it for now.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.210
You should go back to class.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.760
Thank you...

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.470
Oh! Sawamura-kun...

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:43.360
I forgot to thank him.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:53.030
Setsu!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:55.470
What are you doing?

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.520
On my way home from school, that's all.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:58.720
You, Wakana-chan?

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:02.130
I met up with an instrumentalist
I know who lives here.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:02.950
Oh, and...

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:06.670
Here. To celebrate you
starting back at school.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:09.380
<i>A case made of kiri wood!</i>

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:11.640
<i>Wow. You seem really happy with it.</i>

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:16.010
Umeko's your legal guardian
until you graduate.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.280
Make sure you take the monthly allowance
she gives you for living expenses.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.680
This situation... is kind of weird, isn't it?

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.340
Getting a congratulatory gift
from you, Wakana-chan.

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:28.900
If this keeps up, I'll be
questioning why I left home.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:34.150
I think I've started
to understand how you feel.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:39.080
I looked up to Gramps' sound, too.

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:45.330
With Gramps gone, there were only
heavy burdens left for you there.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:51.660
Wakana-chan.

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:52.300
Yeah?

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:55.410
With penguins and seals and stuff,

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.620
the parents recognize
the voices of their offspring.

00:17:57.620 --> 00:18:00.300
even when there are hundreds of them.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.980
Where's this coming from?

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:06.270
I've been thinking about that talk this morning...

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.870
about being good or
bad at performing.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.480
I don't know what makes
a performance good.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:13.640
What I do know for certain is,

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:16.110
even if lots of shamisens
were all being played at once,

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.860
I'd know your sound, Wakana-chan.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.960
That's just because you've got a good ear.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.530
Were you worried I was feeling down?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:27.500
No. It's not like that

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.960
It's not like you to worry
about others, Setsu.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:33.740
I guess it's because
I made you worry, huh?

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:34.810
Sorry.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.080
<i>This is hard.</i>

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.470
Tanukichi Diner

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:49.380
Please look out for my little brother, Setsu.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:45.890
Tanukichi Diner

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:52.940
Sure thing. I'll think of it
like I've gained a son.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.700
Don't worry

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:54.700
Wakana-chan!

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:56.650
Let's play.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.520
Together, I mean. Before you leave.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:01.780
INARI

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:01.780
SHRINE

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:01.790
You always do things out of the blue, don't you?

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:05.160
Setsu-san, I always come here
when I want to play a lot.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.330
Is this an Inari shrine?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.420
Won't the foxes be angry?

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:13.370
The fox spirits are kind. They won't be angry.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.480
We'll only borrow the
space for a little while.

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:18.060
Please listen, if you'd like.

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:22.910
What should we play?

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.800
"Jongara"? "Aiya"?

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:27.930
Nope.

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:31.020
We haven't played <i>that</i> one
in a while. Let's play that.

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:33.560
"That one"?

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:34.980
The piece doesn't have a name.

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:38.910
Wakana-chan and I made it up as kids
when we were messing around.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:23.030
<i>He's always been right behind me.</i>

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.090
<i>I'd run away.</i>

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:32.410
<i>He'd chase after me.</i>

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:34.410
<i>I'd run.</i>

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.390
<i>And run.</i>

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:46.850
Here!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.430
Come here!

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:49.800
Hurry up!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.320
<i>You've caught up, huh?</i>

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.000
Quietly.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:40.380
Quietly?

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:47.530
Won't it feel like it's missing something?

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:52.490
After that, let loose...

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:53.830
<i>...and take flight!</i>

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:57.960
<i>I won't wait for you.</i>

00:21:58.460 --> 00:21:59.760
<i>I'm going on ahead.</i>

00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:04.800
<i>Don't treat me like a fool.
I'll catch up soon enough.</i>

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:09.970
Th-They're amazing.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:16.940
<i>This is the melody... of these two brothers...</i>

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:33.990
Offerings

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:06.820
A transfer student?

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:09.640
He really knows a lot about the shamisen.

00:24:09.640 --> 00:24:11.420
Really? That's great news for you.

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:15.050
Does it seem like he'll join
your appreciation club?

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:18.220
I think I'd be happy if he did.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:20.940
I feel like I'd be able to get
closer to that song that way.
